  "title": "Early Menopause May Raise the Risk of High Blood Pressure, New Study Finds",
  "summary": "Menopause is a natural stage of life that marks the end of a woman's reproductive years. While most women experience menopause between the ages of 45 and 55, some go through it much earlier. According to new research, women who experience menopause before the age of 40 may face a greater risk of developing high blood pressure later in life. The findings add to growing evidence that the timing of menopause plays an important role in long-term cardiovascular health. Researchers believe healthcare",
